"\n\n\n\n\n## Review\nHe opened a bookstore for revenge.  \nOnly this part was fresh. Too predictable a story and too predictable a twist, and revenge scenes that seemed unnecessary.  \n\nI can see what fun elements and twists the author wanted to include, but it's too light and easy.  \n\nThe last part was probably included to give readers a sense of catharsis, but it's just provocative."